# Story 58: Reading Background Output / Killing (40s)
# Hook: Check on a background job with bash_output, and shut it down with kill_shell.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-058-reading-background-output-killing.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Check on a background job with bash_output, and shut it down with kill_shell.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh -- assume a background job is already running here.

[00:08.0 --> 00:13.0]
Double-press Escape for prompt mode.

[00:13.0 --> 00:28.0]
Ask what the background jobs are doing. The bash_output tool reads from a session's ring buffer, or lists every running session if you don't name one. It's read-only, so there's no approval prompt.

[00:28.0 --> 00:37.0]
When you're done, ask it to stop the job. The kill_shell tool terminates the session and returns its final output. Killing is approval-gated -- press y to confirm.

[00:37.0 --> 00:40.0]
Watch it, then end it -- full control over background work.

